        "2": {
            "varname": "countdown_input",
            "caption": "Countdown: Input",
            "description": "One date to count down to, in the format \"Display Name, YYYY-MM-DD, warn, crit\". Both thresholds are a number of days left and may be omitted; \"none\" switches one off, so that state is never returned for that date. A plain number alerts once fewer days than that are left. Supports Nagios ranges. The display name may contain commas, the date field separates it from the thresholds. Can be specified multiple times. Default thresholds: 50/30 days. Example: `--input \"Supermicro SYS1, 2027-01-10, 50, 30\"`.",
